    "name": "Cold plate",
    "category": "stage",
    "parent": "fridge_interior",
    "function": "Gold-plated copper plate that defines the cold plate isotherm of the insert. Every wire passing through is thermally anchored here so that the heat it conducts from the warmer stage is intercepted at this temperature rather than reaching the colder stages. An intermediate anchor at about 100 mK between the still and the mixing chamber, cooled by the returning dilute stream; it is where the readout-line attenuators and the drive_60dB extra attenuator sit.",
